exports[`DetailPanel dispatch matrix > renders memento after data loads 1`] = `
<div>
  <div
    aria-label="Feature details"
    aria-live="polite"
  >
    <div
      class="fixed z-overlay w-80 max-h-[80vh] overflow-y-auto custom-scrollbar rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-surface-primary shadow-2xl"
      style="left: 688px; top: 60px;"
    >
      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-white/5 cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing select-none"
      >
        <span
          class="text-white/65 text-[13px] uppercase tracking-widest mb-1.5 font-sans truncate pr-2 mb-0"
        >
          MEMENTO Cast
        </span>
        <button
          aria-label="Close"
          class="text-white/60 hover:text-white text-lg leading-none transition-colors shrink-0"
        >
          ×
        </button>
      </div>
      <div
        class="px-4 py-4"
      >
        <div
          class="mb-3 px-2 py-1.5 rounded-lg bg-orange-500/10 border-orange-500/20 border"
        >
          <p
            class="text-orange-400 text-[14px] font-sans"
          >
            Platform-derived classification. MEMENTO publishes dissolved and atmospheric gas under the same column name (CH₄ is both Methane_Ocean [nmol/l] and Methane_Atmosphere [ppb]) and its CSV export omits the distinction. Where the contributor did not label a sample 
            <span
              class="font-mono"
            >
              _Air
            </span>
            , we inferred which values are atmospheric from the cruise median; those are marked “air”. The underlying values are unmodified, and every value — including flagged ones — is available in Area Export.
             
            If you intend to publish data from this cast, MEMENTO’s terms of use ask you to cite the database as: Kock, A. and Bange, H. W. (2015) Counting the ocean’s greenhouse gas emissions, Eos 96(3), 10–13, doi:10.1029/2015EO023665 — to include their acknowledgement statement, to also cite the original publications if you use fewer than 10 individual data submissions, and to contact the contributing scientist for permission to use any unpublished data.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span
          class="inline-block text-[14px] font-mono border rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 mb-2 text-teal-300 border-teal-500/40"
